From 0cdd58549405cde1ef4a686b02e97425b533eb57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 03:45:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Make the ontology-ci pre-push hook able to fail, and stop
 it discarding the artifact make ci rebuilt

The `ontology-ci` hook had two defects that both presented as a green run.

It could not fail. The `entry` chain ended `git checkout --
docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json || true`, and a shell returns the status of
the last command in the list, so the hook returned that trailing `|| true`
and exited 0 for every build. Measured against a deliberately broken
ontology (a `gcdfo:` class with no `gcdfo:theme`, which trips
`theme-coverage`): `make ci` exits 2 and the hook reported `Passed`, exit 0.
The gate had never failed for anybody since it was introduced.

It discarded a build product. `make ci` regenerates
`docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json` -- the path is inside `CI_ARTIFACT_PATHS`
-- and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` rejects any uncommitted change left after
`make ci`. The hook's `files` pattern restricts it to changes to
`ontology/dfo-salmon.ttl`, which is exactly when that artifact is expected
to change, so the hook threw away locally what CI then demanded and left the
tree with three regenerated docs artifacts and one reset to HEAD.

The fix captures the build's status in `ci_status`, runs the restore only on
the failure path, and exits with `ci_status`. The failure-path restore is
kept deliberately: `docs-widoco` rsyncs raw WIDOCO output over that path
before the normalizer runs, so a build that dies in between leaves raw
generator bytes a later run would adopt as its normalizer baseline and go
green over. Restoring on failure is the remedy `docs/tech-debt.md`
prescribes under its 2026-08-16 entry, which says to run it before retrying
a FAILED docs build rather than after every push -- so this half needed no
wait on that entry's own fix.

The comment block on the hook carries both rules and the retirement
condition for the failure branch: it goes when the 2026-08-16 tech-debt
entry retires, because that fix makes `docs-widoco` restore the pre-run
bytes itself and leaves nothing for the branch to do.

Evidence, all against the same deliberately broken ontology or the same
label edit:
  - broken ontology, before: `Passed`, pre-commit exit 0
  - broken ontology, after:  `Failed`, `exit code: 2`, pre-commit exit 1
  - valid ontology edit, before: `docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json` absent
    from the post-hook tree
  - valid ontology edit, after:  present, and `make ci-sync-artifacts`
    stages all four artifacts
  - clean valid tree, after: `Passed`, exit 0, tree untouched
  - dirtied `ontology.json` plus a failing build, after: restored, and the
    hook still exits 2

Refs hub queue item B-150.
